# Emperor penguin

The emperor penguin is the largest living penguin and the only one that breeds
through the Antarctic winter, on fast ice far from open water. It takes
Antarctic silverfish, squid and krill while submerged, propelling itself through
the water with its flippers on descents that routinely pass two hundred metres
and last up to twenty minutes. Haemoglobin with a high affinity for oxygen, a
collapsible ribcage and a lowered heart rate make such an excursion survivable.
The male incubates the single egg on his feet for two months without food. See
[[spheniscidae]].
